# macOS capture

The helper and the Go adapter are one boundary. Follow the macOS capture section in `AGENTS.md` and `internal/capture/macos/README.md`.

- The desktop app sets 2-second chunks in `platform_source_darwin.go`. Swift's `CaptureDefaults.chunkSeconds` matches that. Utterance windows are assembled in `internal/service/capture_pipeline.go`.
- Helper commands are `list`, `capture`, and `stop`. `capture` requires `--bundle-id` and `--spool`.
- Keep the non-Darwin stubs building. The real adapter is `//go:build darwin`.
- `swift test` needs full Xcode. `./scripts/verify.sh` skips it when `xctest` is absent and fails when `xctest` is present and tests fail.
